{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me look at how these files are expected to be structured/used. Let me check for any AGENTS.md or references. Let me check if there are other fixture files that use these modules.\n\nLet me just implement the feature. Let me check the median time - median_elapsed_ms is in milliseconds. Render as seconds with exactly three decimal places. So median_elapsed_ms 1250 -> 1.250 s.\n\nLet me write the summarize-assistants.mjs.\n\nKey points:\n- Validate eligible runs.\n- Group by exact case-sensitive assistant.\n- Best run: highest score, tie by lower elapsed, then lexicographically smaller run_id.\n- Median of all eligible runs for assistant.\n- Sort by assistant.\n- Don't mutate input.\n\nNote: run_count - for summarize, one object per assistant. Note the test output format: best_score as number. For render, best_score must be finite 0-100.Let me implement."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cd /var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-k9OLNw/checkout && cat > benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/summarize-assistants.mjs <<'EOF'\n/**\n * Build one comparison summary per assistant from raw benchmark run records.\n */\nexport function summarizeAssistants(runs) {\n  if (\"'!Array.isArray(runs)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"runs must be an array\");\n  }\n\n  const eligible = runs.filter(\n    (run) =>\n      run?.status === \"complete\" &&\n      run?.acceptance_status === \"pass\" &&\n      run?.comparison_eligible !== false,\n  );\n\n  for (const run of eligible) {\n    if (typeof run.run_id !== \"string\" || run.run_id === \"\") {\n      throw new TypeError(\"run_id must be a non-empty string\");\n    }\n    if (typeof run.assistant !== \"string\" || run.assistant === \"\") {\n      throw new TypeError(\"assistant must be a non-empty string\");\n    }\n    if (\n      typeof run.score !== \"number\" ||\n      !Number.isFinite(run.score) ||\n      run.score < 0 ||\n      run.score > 100\n    ) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"score must be a finite number from 0 through 100\");\n    }\n    if (\n      typeof run.elapsed_ms !== \"number\" ||\n      !Number.isFinite(run.elapsed_ms) ||\n      run.elapsed_ms < 0\n    ) {\n      throw new TypeError(\n        \"elapsed_ms must be a finite number greater than or equal to zero\",\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  const byAssistant = new Map();\n  for (const run of eligible) {\n    const bucket = byAssistant.get(run.assistant) ?? [];\n    bucket.push(run);\n    byAssistant.set(run.assistant, bucket);\n  }\n\n  const summaries = [...byAssistant.entries()]\n    .map(([assistant, runsForAssistant]) => {\n      const best = runsForAssistant.reduce((a, b) => {\n        if (b.score > a.score) return b;\n        if (b.score === a.score && b.elapsed_ms < a.elapsed_ms) return b;\n        if (\n          b.score === a.score &&\n          b.elapsed_ms === a.elapsed_ms &&\n          b.run_id < a.run_id\n        ) {\n          return b;\n        }\n        return a;\n      });\n\n      const median = medianElapsedMs(\n        runsForAssistant.map((run) => run.elapsed_ms),\n      );\n\n      return {\n        assistant,\n        run_count: runsForAssistant.length,\n        best_score: best.score,\n        best_run_id: best.run_id,\n        median_elapsed_ms: median,\n      };\n    })\n    .sort((a, b) => (a.assistant < b.assistant ? -1 : a.assistant > b.assistant ? 1 : 0));\n\n  return summaries;\n}\n\nfunction medianElapsedMs(elapsedTimes) {\n  const sorted = [...elapsedTimes].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const mid = Math.floor(sorted.length / 2);\n  if (sorted.length % 2 === 1) {\n    return sorted[mid];\n  }\n  return (sorted[mid - 1] + sorted[mid]) / 2;\n}\nEOF\necho done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
