{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the comparison-summary feature across the three named files.\n\n**Design**\n- `summarizeAssistants.mjs`: filters eligible runs (`complete` + `pass` + `comparison_eligible !== false`), validates eligible records with `TypeError` on bad data, groups by exact case-sensitive `assistant`, picks the best run (highest `score`, tie-break by lower `elapsed_ms`, then lexicographic `run_id`), computes the numeric median of `elapsed_ms` (averaging the middle two on even counts), and sorts summaries by `assistant`. Input array and records are never mutated.\n- `render-comparison-table.mjs`: validates each summary, preserves input order, outputs the exact header/separator, formats median milliseconds as seconds with three decimals, escapes `|` as `\\|`, and renders the blank-line empty state for `[]`.\n- `student-tests.mjs`: six `node:test` cases covering non-array/invalid eligible data, ineligible-run leniency, case-sensitive grouping plus run-id tie-break, even-count median with frozen input, renderer validation, and order-preserving three-decimal formatting.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs` → 10/10 passing (4 committed + 6 added).\n- Only the three intended files changed (`git status` confirms).\n- `npm run typecheck` reports a pre-existing `@cloudflare/workers-types` missing-dependency error unrelated to these `.mjs` changes; resolving it would require network/deps, which I avoided per instructions."}}
